 "268": {
  "inputs": {
   "prompt": "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Hyper realistic cinematic footage, ultra detailed, volumetric light, shallow depth of field. A dim arcade in the year 2050, worn carpet and scuffed floor panels lit by a mix of old fluorescent tubes and cyan and magenta neon. A teenage boy stands on a circular haptic platform wearing a slim black visor and glowing bands on his wrists and ankles, knees bent, shoulders shifting as he plays. Two other players stand in identical rigs glowing further back, and a paper soda cup sits on the platform rail. The camera pushes slowly and steadily toward him across the room, closing gradually on the visor until reflections of a rain lit neon city crawl across its black mirrored surface, and keeps pushing until the visor fills the entire frame. A burst of electric blue light floods the frame to white. The white clears to a first person point of view inside the game, sleek grey gloved hands and forearms swinging in frame, sprinting hard along a wet rooftop high above a vast neon megacity with rain streaking sideways. The view sprints straight at the roof edge and launches off it in one long flat leap, staying level rather than dropping, gloved hands thrown forward, flying forward between two towers toward a rooftop directly ahead at the same height, the glowing street far below.\n\noverall_soundscape: Low arcade hum, cooling fans and distant muffled game audio, echoing pop music playing through old ceiling speakers and reverberating across the room, the boy breathing fast, soft servo clicks from the haptic rig, then a deep bass whoosh as the sound swaps to roaring wind, hard fast footfalls slapping wet metal, rain, and the launch into open air where the footsteps stop and only wind remains.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: No score during the arcade, then a driving electronic score with pulsing synth bass entering as the white light clears.",
