 "269": {
  "inputs": {
   "prompt": "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Hyper realistic cinematic first person point of view video game footage, ultra detailed, volumetric light, wide angle with motion blur. Sleek grey gloved hands and forearms are thrown forward in frame, flying forward in one long flat leap between two towers in a vast neon megacity, level with a rooftop directly ahead at the same height, rain streaking past, the glowing street far below. The rooftop rushes up and the view slams down onto it, dropping hard and low as the legs absorb the impact and the gloved hands swing down out of frame, then rising smoothly back to running height as the sprint continues forward without pausing. An enormous hovering transport ship roars across low overhead from left to right, its lit underside filling the entire top of the frame, engine downwash blasting the rain sideways and tearing ripples across the puddles on the roof as the view flinches down and keeps running beneath it. Ahead is the edge of the rooftop and beyond it is a thick metal pipe connecting the edge of the roof with the edge of the roof 10 feet away. The view slows and glances down as the player's feet take confident precise steps onto the pipe connecting the roofs, the city streets coming into view far far below, a high speed train track seen to the left of the current building. And then the view looks back up, moving forward deliberately as the next rooftop approaches. Suddenly a trap door opens and a man in dark military gear and a heavy weapon emerges and points at the viewer yelling through the rain [English]<d>Runner! Stop immediately!\"</d>, voice drowned out slightly by the rain and pulsing beat. The video ends while the viewer is still moving forward on the pipe between buildings, nearing the next rooftop.\n\noverall_soundscape: Roaring wind and rain with no footsteps through the flight, then a heavy crashing impact of boots on wet metal and a grunt of effort, fast pounding footfalls resuming, then a colossal engine roar building and passing directly overhead with a deep thrumming downwash that drowns everything, the roar receding, footfalls hammering, the the sound of slightly straining metal, footfalls on the hollow metal, and breathing as the pipe crossing begins.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A driving electronic score at full intensity, pulsing synth bass and tight percussion under a soaring synth lead that continues throughout the video.",
