 "270": {
  "inputs": {
   "prompt": "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Hyper realistic cinematic first person point of view video game footage, ultra detailed, volumetric light, wide angle with motion blur. Sleek grey gloved hands are in frame as the player cross a metal pipe connecting two rooftops, with a man in dark military gear seen pointing a heavy weapon at the viewer. The view leaps into running motion as the view crosses over to the next rooftop, then banks sharply left avoiding the man. The view runs forward and skids to a halt right near the next edge. The view looks down for a moment at a futuristic hyper fast train that is speeding past just below the level of the rooftop, left to right. The view looks left down the track, seeing the train stretching and winding through the city, and then glances right to see the train speeding towards some tall neon-lit buildings. A voice is heard from behind, yelling but drowned out by the rain: [English]<d>Nowhere to run!</d>.  After a moment's hesitation the view looks forward again and leaps onto the train, the gloved fist seen grabbing hard on a metal handhold on the roof of the fast moving train, and the view whips with motion blur as it steadies itself. At the very end the view stabilizes and stands, looking forward from the roof of the train, looking up at the beautiful city of even taller buildings in the rainy night. As buildings near the train whip by in a blur of motion there is a moment of reflection.\n\noverall_soundscape: Metal creaking slightly under footfalls and then rapid footsteps on wet concrete. Then the deep roar and rhythmic clatter of a train at full speed, screeching metal wheels on the track. The sound of a breath intake and the sudden transition to the roaring wind sound as the player jumps onto the train, rain hammering on metal, wind tearing past, hard breathing gradually steadying under it all.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A driving electronic score that lands on a final small synth piano melody at the very end as the viewer stands on the train, opening out wide as the skyline is revealed.",
